S3. CONDITIONS OF USE
================================================================================

3.1  Attribution

     Any distribution of the Software or Derivative Works, whether in source
     or binary form, must retain:

       (i)    the original copyright notice:
              "Copyright (C) 2026 QPT";
       (ii)   this License in its entirety, or a prominent notice directing
              recipients to the full text of the License;
       (iii)  a clear indication of any modifications made to the Software
              relative to the original version.

     Removal or obscuring of the copyright notice is a violation subject to
     the consequences in S11.

3.2  Share-Alike for Modifications

     If you distribute a Derivative Work, you must:

       (i)    make the source code of your modifications publicly available
              under this License or a compatible license approved in writing
              by QPT;
       (ii)   provide a written Modification Disclosure -- a summary describing
              the nature and scope of the modifications, NOT required to reveal
              proprietary algorithms, trade secrets, or other intellectual
              property not itself derived from the Software;
       (iii)  submit the Modification Disclosure to QPT by opening a public
              issue or pull request in the official QPT-LLM repository, or
              by sending it to the designated QPT contact address.

     Modification Disclosure does NOT require disclosure of:
       (a) proprietary data pipelines used for training;
       (b) internal tooling not derived from the Software; or
       (c) business-confidential information unrelated to the Software.

3.3  Open Deployment of Trained Models

     If you train a Model using the Software and deploy it publicly --
     including via an API, web service, or downloadable release -- you must:

       (i)    make the Model weights publicly available, or provide a
              documented mechanism for others to reproduce training under
              comparable conditions;
       (ii)   include attribution to QPT in any public-facing model card,
              paper, or documentation associated with the Model;
       (iii)  comply with the dataset licensing requirements in S6.

     You are NOT required to open-source the Model if it is used solely for
     internal, non-commercial purposes.


