================================================================================
S5. COMMERCIAL USE
================================================================================

5.1  Permitted Commercial Use

     Commercial Use of the Software is permitted subject to this section.
     Any entity engaging in Commercial Use must:

       (a) comply with all attribution and share-alike conditions in S3;
       (b) not misrepresent the origin or nature of the Software;
       (c) include a disclosure in product documentation or terms of service
           stating that the product incorporates QPT.

5.2  Large Commercial User Obligation

     A Large Commercial User must, on an annual basis, make a direct monetary
     donation to QPT.

     The economic value of the donation must be proportional to the revenue
     generated from the product or service that incorporates or relies upon
     the Software, a Model trained using the Software, or a Derivative Work.

     QPT will publish a contribution schedule specifying suggested amounts
     based on revenue tiers. The applicable contribution amount for each
     annual period shall be determined according to the QPT contribution
     schedule applicable to that annual period and the applicable revenue tier
     of the Large Commercial User.

     The relevant revenue for purposes of determining the applicable revenue
     tier shall be the Annual Gross Revenue attributable to the product or
     service that incorporates or relies upon the Software, a Model trained
     using the Software, or a Derivative Work, as defined in S1.

     A Large Commercial User shall provide QPT, upon reasonable request,
     sufficient financial, accounting, commercial, or other reliable
     information reasonably necessary to determine the applicable revenue
     tier and contribution amount.

     QPT shall not require disclosure of information that is not reasonably
     necessary to determine the applicable revenue tier or contribution
     amount. Commercially sensitive information provided to QPT for this
     purpose may be provided confidentially and shall be used for the purpose
     of determining compliance with this Section.

     Revenue and the applicable revenue tier may be determined using
     financial statements, accounting records, sales records, commercial
     records, or other reliable evidence reasonably available to the Large
     Commercial User and QPT.

     If the revenue attributable to the relevant product or service cannot
     reasonably be determined with precision, QPT and the Large Commercial
     User shall cooperate in good faith to determine a reasonable attributable
     revenue amount and applicable revenue tier using the reliable evidence
     reasonably available to the parties.

     This obligation applies equally to Commercial Use in the Training Phase
     (i.e., using the Software to train a Model that is subsequently used
     commercially, even if the Software itself is not redistributed).

     The USD $5,000,000 threshold and all monetary amounts in this License are
     denominated in United States Dollars as of 2026 and adjusted annually
     using the applicable CPI as described in S1.

QPT may provide general information and advisory guidance regarding R&D tax
incentives, research grants, fiscal programs, and other governmental programs
that may be relevant to organizations conducting or supporting research.
Nothing in this License requires or guarantees any tax reduction, tax credit,
or fiscal benefit.


