S10. COMMERCIAL VIOLATION DAMAGES AND CONTRACTUAL PENALTY
================================================================================

Any material violation of the commercial use obligations in S5 shall constitute
a material breach of this License and shall be subject to the following
contractual remedies, to the maximum extent permitted by applicable Colombian
law.

10.1 Contractual Penalty

The parties expressly agree to a contractual penalty (cláusula penal
sancionatoria) pursuant to Articles 1592 and following of the Colombian Civil
Code, including Articles 1592, 1594, 1595, 1596, 1599, 1600, and 1601,
as applicable.

In the event of a material breach of the commercial use obligations in S5,
including unauthorized Commercial Use or failure to comply with the
obligations applicable to a Large Commercial User, the breaching party
shall be obligated to pay QPT a contractual penalty equal to three (3)
times the economic benefit obtained by the breaching party as a result
of such breach.

10.2 Economic Benefit

For purposes of this Section, "economic benefit" means the economic
benefit reasonably attributable to the unauthorized or non-compliant
commercial use giving rise to the breach. The amount shall be determined
on the basis of available financial, accounting, commercial, or other
reliable evidence.

10.3 Legal Character of the Penalty

The parties expressly agree that the amount established in this Section
constitutes a cláusula penal within the meaning of Article 1592 of the
Colombian Civil Code and is intended to secure compliance with the
commercial obligations established in this License and to establish the
contractual consequences of a material breach.

The contractual penalty shall be subject to the mandatory provisions of
Colombian law, including Articles 1594, 1595, 1596, 1599, 1600, and 1601
of the Colombian Civil Code, as applicable.

10.4 Contractual Penalty and Indemnification of Damages

The parties expressly agree, pursuant to Article 1600 of the Colombian
Civil Code, that QPT may demand both the contractual penalty established
in this Section and the indemnification of damages caused by the breach.

Accordingly, payment of the contractual penalty shall not, by itself,
release the breaching party from its obligation to indemnify QPT for
additional damages caused by the breach, including damages exceeding
the amount of the contractual penalty, to the extent such damages are
proven and recoverable under applicable Colombian law.

The contractual penalty and the indemnification of damages shall
constitute separate contractual remedies. QPT shall not be required to
waive the contractual penalty in order to seek indemnification of
additional damages.

Nothing in this Section shall permit double recovery of the same damage
or loss. The breaching party shall remain liable for the contractual
penalty and, where applicable, for the additional damages actually
caused by the breach, subject to the mandatory provisions of Colombian
law.

10.5 Determination of Economic Benefit and Damages

Any dispute concerning the existence of the breach, the economic benefit
obtained, the amount of the contractual penalty, the existence or amount
of additional damages, or any applicable reduction or limitation under
Colombian law shall be determined in accordance with the arbitration
provisions of S14.

10.6 Other Remedies

The contractual penalty does not prevent QPT from seeking termination of
the License, cessation of unauthorized use, injunctive or protective
measures where legally available, or other remedies available under
applicable Colombian law.

Nothing in this Section shall be interpreted as waiving or limiting any
mandatory limitation, judicial or arbitral power of reduction, or other
protection applicable to contractual penalties under Colombian law.


