S11. TERMINATION
================================================================================

11.1  Grounds for Termination

      Your rights under this License terminate automatically if:

        (a) you fail to cure a violation subject to a cure period (see S11.3)
            within the applicable time limit;
        (b) you commit a violation for which no cure period is provided;
        (c) you initiate patent litigation against QPT or any contributor
            as described in S9.3;
        (d) you make a material misrepresentation regarding attribution,
            Modification Disclosure, or commercial use status.

11.2  Effect of Termination

      Upon termination of this License:

        (a) all rights granted to you under this License cease immediately;
        (b) you must cease all use, distribution, and sublicensing of the
            Software and any Derivative Works;
        (c) you must destroy or return to QPT all copies of the Software in
            your possession or control, to the extent technically practicable;
        (d) sublicenses previously granted by you to third parties in
            compliance with this License survive termination, provided those
            third parties independently comply with this License;
        (e) obligations that by their nature should survive termination
            (including S10, S12, S13, S14, and S15) shall survive.

      A party whose license has been terminated may not obtain a new license
      from QPT -- whether directly or through an affiliate -- without prior
      written authorization from QPT. QPT may impose conditions on
      reinstatement, including payment of damages or other remedial measures.

11.3  Cure Periods and Violation Consequences

      Violation                              Consequence
      --------------------------------       ------------------------------------------------
      Minor attribution error                30 days to correct; license continues if cured.
      Failure to share modifications         Immediate termination.
      Unauthorized commercial use            Immediate termination + damages + penalty (S10).
      Removal of copyright notice            15 days to correct; license continues if cured.
      Deliberate fraud                       Immediate termination + possible damages.


