S14. GOVERNING LAW AND JURISDICTION
================================================================================

14.1 Governing Law

     This License shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the
     laws of the Republic of Colombia, without regard to its conflict of law
     provisions.

14.2 Arbitration Agreement

     Any dispute, controversy, difference, claim, or disagreement arising out
     of or relating to this License, including its existence, validity,
     interpretation, execution, performance, breach, termination, or
     consequences thereof, as well as any dispute concerning rights or
     obligations arising from or in connection with the Software, shall be
     finally resolved by arbitration.

14.3 Arbitration Institution

     The arbitration shall be administered by the Centro de Conciliación,
     Arbitraje y Amigable Composición de la Cámara de Comercio de Medellín
     para Antioquia, in accordance with the arbitration rules of that Center
     in force at the time the arbitration is commenced, except to the extent
     that the parties expressly agree otherwise or applicable Colombian law
     requires otherwise.

14.4 Number and Appointment of Arbitrators

     The arbitral tribunal shall be composed of three (3) arbitrators.

The three (3) arbitrators shall be appointed by the Centro de Conciliación, Arbitraje y Amigable Composición de la Cámara de Comercio de Medellín para Antioquia by means of a draw (sorteo) from its applicable lists of arbitrators, in accordance with the applicable rules and procedures of the Center.

 The appointment of the arbitrators by the Center shall be conducted in accordance with Colombian arbitration law and the applicable regulations of the Centro de Conciliación, Arbitraje y Amigable Composición de la Cámara de Comercio de Medellín para Antioquia.

14.5 Arbitration in Law

     The arbitral tribunal shall decide the dispute in law (arbitraje en
     derecho), applying the applicable substantive law and the mandatory
     procedural rules of the Republic of Colombia.

14.6 Seat and Place of Arbitration

     The legal seat of the arbitration shall be Medellín, Antioquia,
     Republic of Colombia. The arbitration shall be administered by the
     Centro de Conciliación, Arbitraje y Amigable Composición de la Cámara
     de Comercio de Medellín para Antioquia.

14.7 Final and Binding Award

     The arbitral award shall be final and binding upon the parties, subject
     only to the remedies and grounds for challenge or annulment expressly
     permitted under applicable Colombian law.

14.8 Scope of Arbitration Agreement

     This arbitration agreement is independent and separable from the other
     provisions of this License. The existence, validity, effectiveness, or
     termination of this License shall not, by itself, affect the validity or
     enforceability of this arbitration agreement.

14.9 Judicial Jurisdiction Excluded

     Except for those judicial functions expressly reserved to Colombian courts
     by mandatory provisions of Colombian arbitration law, the parties
     expressly exclude the jurisdiction and competence of the ordinary
     Colombian courts with respect to any dispute, controversy, difference,
     claim, or disagreement falling within the scope of this arbitration
     agreement.

     The parties therefore agree that such disputes shall be resolved
     exclusively and finally by the arbitral tribunal constituted in
     accordance with this Section. Judicial intervention shall be limited to
     those matters that cannot lawfully be submitted to arbitration or that
     Colombian law expressly assigns to the courts in connection with the
     arbitration.

14.10 Applicable Arbitration Law

     The arbitration shall be conducted in accordance with the applicable
     provisions of Colombian arbitration law, including Law 1563 of 2012, as
     amended or replaced from time to time, together with the applicable
     regulations of the Centro de Conciliación, Arbitraje y Amigable
     Composición de la Cámara de Comercio de Medellín para Antioquia.

14.11 Language

     The arbitration shall be conducted in Spanish, unless the parties
     otherwise agree or the arbitral tribunal determines otherwise in
     accordance with the applicable rules of the Center.


